    "tagline": "Last the night against the parade of a hundred demons",
    "category": "fun",
    "play": true,
    "platforms": [
      "macos",
      "linux"
    ],
    "actions": [
      {
        "title": "Move",
        "description": "WASD too.",
        "keys": "up, down, left, right"
      },
      {
        "title": "Smoke dash",
        "description": "A short burst you can't be hurt in.",
        "keys": "space"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pick at a level-up",
        "description": "Or the arrows and Enter; R rerolls, X skips, B banishes.",
        "keys": "1, 2, 3"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pause",
        "description": "Your build and stats; Q gives up the night.",
        "keys": "esc"
      },
      {
        "title": "Sound on or off",
        "keys": "m"
      }
    ],
    "features": [
      "A fifteen-minute night in three acts (Dusk, Midnight, the Hour of the Ox), each with its own crowd, scripted events and a boss: the Tanuki, the Tengu, and the Oni at the head of the parade",
      "Sixteen weapons, each with its own job, eight levels and an evolution when paired with the right item; sixteen items; reroll, skip and banish at level-ups",
      "Six heroes with a starting weapon and a trait, four of them unlocked by playing",
      "Telegraphed danger: rings and lines on the ground before a slam or a charge, a smoke dash to get out",
      "A blessing to choose as Midnight and the Hour of the Ox begin: more damage, more projectiles, more area, armor, healing or speed for the rest of the night",
      "A shrine for lasting upgrades between nights, a codex of everything found and defeated, and omens for harder nights once you've seen the dawn",
      "Leaderboards for each hero's longest night, the fastest dawn and the most demons defeated; signed in, your gold, shrine, unlocks and codex follow you to your other machines and play.cagdas.io"
    ],
